# Builds and runs the landing-page SSR server (refactor #334). Serves `/` server-rendered
# and falls back to the static SPA shell for every other route. Standalone image — a
# sibling infra PR provisions the actual deploy target; this just needs to run anywhere:
#
#   docker build -f Dockerfile.ssr -t notism-web-ssr .
#   docker run -p 3000:3000 notism-web-ssr
#   curl http://localhost:3000/

FROM oven/bun:1.1-alpine AS builder

WORKDIR /app

RUN apk add --no-cache libc6-compat

COPY package.json bun.lockb ./
# `--ignore-scripts`: skips the `prepare` (husky) script — there's no `.git` in this
# build context (see `.dockerignore`) for it to hook into.
RUN bun install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts

COPY . .

# Builds the client + SSR bundles directly with Vite, skipping the `tsc -b` project-wide
# typecheck that `build:client`/`build:ssr` normally run first — that typecheck also covers
# `test/` + every `__tests__/` folder (tsconfig.app.json), which the root `.dockerignore`
# (shared with the plain dev `Dockerfile`, which never typechecks) excludes from this build
# context. Type safety is already enforced by CI's `bun run build`/`bun run test` outside
# Docker; this image only needs valid build output.
RUN bunx vite build --outDir dist/client && VITE_SSR_BUILD=true bunx vite build --ssr src/entry-server.tsx --outDir dist/server

FROM oven/bun:1.1-alpine AS runner

WORKDIR /app

RUN apk add --no-cache libc6-compat

ENV NODE_ENV=production
ENV PORT=3000

COPY package.json bun.lockb ./
RUN bun install --frozen-lockfile --production --ignore-scripts

COPY --from=builder /app/dist/client ./dist/client
COPY --from=builder /app/dist/server ./dist/server
COPY server.ts ./

EXPOSE 3000

CMD ["bun", "run", "server.ts"]
